WEBVTT

00:03.070 --> 00:04.980
Could you show me?

00:06.150 --> 00:07.520
<b>Konkon</b>

00:08.900 --> 00:12.040
Um, Director...

00:12.780 --> 00:17.320
Episode 5: JUSTICE

00:13.130 --> 00:18.860
We're at the point where we really need the 
storyboards for Part A or we'll be in trouble.

00:17.800 --> 00:18.860
When?

00:18.860 --> 00:20.530
You mean the deadline?

00:20.750 --> 00:22.890
We're already way past it.

00:22.890 --> 00:24.080
First love.

00:25.710 --> 00:27.430
Your first love.

00:27.740 --> 00:30.050
I've already told you about it.

00:30.050 --> 00:30.870
When?

00:31.450 --> 00:33.420
My second year of middle school.

00:33.780 --> 00:34.850
How'd you meet?

00:35.300 --> 00:37.750
We were both in concert band.

00:38.150 --> 00:39.590
Your first love...

00:42.020 --> 00:43.020
<b>Konkon</b>

00:43.800 --> 00:45.260
Could you show me?

00:45.800 --> 00:46.890
Go on.

00:48.790 --> 00:53.130
B-But I can't draw...

00:53.130 --> 00:57.000
There's the terrifying hunt
 for first love again.

00:57.000 --> 00:58.270
Hunt for first love?

00:58.270 --> 01:00.030
If you talk to the director,

01:00.030 --> 01:03.040
she'll sit you down right there,

01:03.040 --> 01:07.800
and make you draw every detail of your
first love before she'll let you go.

01:07.800 --> 01:09.030
Yikes.

01:09.040 --> 01:11.050
<b>Director / Natsuko Hirose</b>

01:09.040 --> 01:11.050
<b>Opening Next Spring</b>

01:09.040 --> 01:11.050
<b>Today Is Yesterday,
Tomorrow Is Now,
And Every Day Is Summer.</b>

01:09.040 --> 01:11.050
<b>HATSUKOI:
 First Love</b>

01:09.050 --> 01:11.050
<b>Sukeban Magical Girl
Dark Academy</b>

01:09.050 --> 01:11.050
<b>Sukeban Magical Girl
Dark Academy</b>

01:09.050 --> 01:11.050
<b>Sukeban Magical Girl
Dark Academy</b>

01:09.510 --> 01:14.330
Apparently, our company's 
done for if this thing flops.

01:15.680 --> 01:19.260
If it flops like <i>A Tale of Perishing</i>...

01:19.260 --> 01:23.200
Come on. It's not gonna flop that badly.

01:23.620 --> 01:25.180
Yeah, you're right.

01:25.620 --> 01:28.720
I mean, this has the genius 
Natsuko Hirose behind it.

01:30.270 --> 01:34.670
I guess every single person's experience 
is different when it comes to first love.

01:36.030 --> 01:40.770
Research is very important, but people are 
wailing at me that we're gonna be in trouble

01:40.770 --> 01:44.660
if the storyboards aren't done soon. 
You already have a lot on your plate, Natsuko.

01:44.660 --> 01:47.160
Why don't we let someone <i>else</i>
 do the storyboards?

01:47.160 --> 01:48.490
I'll do it all myself.

01:48.490 --> 01:49.290
Huh?

01:49.290 --> 01:51.670
It'll just be faster in the end.

01:51.670 --> 01:53.600
I know, right?

01:53.600 --> 01:57.650
I'll set these clam lunches down right over 
there, so be sure to eat one, honey bun!

